# Architecture boundaries

## Layering

- CLI and TUI call `SpellSyncService` (`spell_sync/application/service.py`) — not core writers directly
- Application layer orchestrates; it must not import Textual
- Core owns mutation semantics: `sync_run`, `push_prepared`, `push_transaction`, `pull`, `project_setup`
- TUI must not import dictionary writers, journal internals, snapshot writers, or config writers

## Immutability and reports

- Prepared preview objects remain frozen through confirmation and execution
- `ReportScreen` displays results — it does not write history or mutate filesystem state
- Do not add a second implementation of an existing execution path

## Canonical references

- `@docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — module map, Pull/Push model
- `@docs/TUI_IMPLEMENTATION.md` — controller, workers, screen routing
